    "evidence_text": "One attempt towards QA of spoken content is TOEFL listening comprehension by machine  .\n\nRecently ODSQA, a SQA corpus recorded by real speakers, is released  .\n\nFIGREF1 .\n\nHence, we can collect source domain data more easily, and adapt the model to the target domain.\n\nWe used the standard evaluation script from SQuAD  to evaluate the performance.\n\nQuestion Answering Model\tThe used architecture of the QA model is briefly summarized below.\n\nperformance on SQuAD.\n\nThe network architecture is illustrated in Figure FIGREF2 .\n\nDomain Adaptation Approach\tThe main focus of this paper is to apply domain adaptation for SQA.\n\nBecause the parameters of other layers in QA model are independent to the loss of the domain discriminator,\n\nThe reference transcriptions are from SQuAD  .\n\nWhile in the testing stage, we evaluate the\n\nperformance on Spoken-SQuAD testing set.\n\nAll models used in the experiments are trained with batch size 20, using adam with learning rate INLINEFORM0 and the early stop strategy.\n\nThe setup is slightly different but better than the setting suggested by the original QAnet.\n\nResults\tFirst, we highlight the domain mismatch phenomenon in our experiments shown in Table TABREF9 .\n\nRow (a) is when QANet is trained on Text-SQuAD, row\n\nThe columns show the evaluation on the testing sets of Text-SQuAD and Spoken-SQuAD.\n\nThe performance gap is nearly 20% F1 score (72% to 55%).\n\nWe also compare to the approach proposed by Lan et al.  in the row (d).\n\nThis approach is originally proposed for spoken language\n\nunderstanding, and we adopt the same approach on the setting here.\n\nThe domain-general parameters are adversarially trained by domain discriminator.\n\nTherefore, our following experiments contain domain adversarial learning.\n\nDifferent combinations\n\nare investigated and shown in Table TABREF14 .\n\nConclusion\tIn this work, we incorporate a domain discriminator to align the\n\nmismatched domains between ASR hypotheses and reference transcriptions.",
